# 003-gc-innermost-frame-under-compiled-code
#
# A collection made while compiled code is live does not report the
# reference slots of the innermost frame — the frame that asked for
# the allocation — as roots. Wrong only when such a frame holds the
# last reference to something it reads after the collection.
#
# An artificial defect for measuring the fuzzing harness (issue 681).
# Never applied to this tree: scripts/fuzz-mutant.sh applies it in a
# scratch worktree. docs/FUZZ_EVALUATION.md records what found it.
diff --git a/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs b/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs
--- a/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs
+++ b/crates/cove-runtime/src/vm/exec.rs
@@ -173,9 +173,12 @@
